# Key Takeaways

- File Explorer is the primary Windows file management tool.
- Task Manager helps monitor system performance and restart Windows Explorer.
- Recycle Bin allows recovery of accidentally deleted files.
- Settings and Control Panel both configure Windows but serve different purposes.
- SSH provides secure remote access.
- SCP securely transfers files.
- NAT allows Private IP addresses to communicate over the Internet.
- Professional troubleshooting always starts with gathering information before applying a solution.

